    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d714">

                <pb facs="0659" n="575" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg575"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 860d.48/3a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor for the Department of State</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Polk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Commercial Adviser of
                        the British Embassy</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crawford</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 12, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Crawford</hi>: The Secretary is of the opinion that certain
                    definite food supplies for Finland should be allowed to go forward to replace
                    flour which had been purchased by the Finnish Senate and which was subsequently
                    requisitioned here.</p>
                <p>It will, of course, be necessary to work out safeguards for the delivery of food
                    supplies. For this purpose, and also to obtain the least possible delay, I have
                    asked Mr. Basil Miles<anchor n="1" xml:id="d714-f1"/> to
                    confer with you, the Food Administration and the War Trade Board. The <pb
                        facs="0660" n="576" xml:id="pg576"/> Finnish Commissioner here assures us
                    that Finnish authorities will do everything practicable to cooperate.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank L. Polk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
